# The loop workspace is its own git repository (the state branch claude/loop-state of the
# project's remote). Its append-only files merge as a union, so two sessions that each append
# records or log entries never conflict; `loop-setup sync` runs `loop-setup lint` before it pushes.
# Rotation (`loop-setup rotate`) is done by one session only — a union of two rotations duplicates.
trace/records.jsonl merge=union
trace/*.jsonl merge=union
loop-run-log.md merge=union
log.md merge=union
